```

adds `e_phnum` of either the `Elf32_Phdr` or `Elf64_Phdr` struct, depending on whether `register_size == REGISTER_32_SIZE` or not. One inconsistent thing is thus that it always in fact advances the offset by PHENTSIZE_32 (32) or PHENTSIZE_64 (56), depending on what is in the `EI_CLASS` byte, but when filling out `segment_info[area_counter].size` and the number of bytes covered by the `ph_entry_tree` subtree in `proto_tree_add_subtree_format`, it uses the value obtained from `e_phentsize`, which might not match.

